WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.963
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module.

2
00:00:02.963 --> 00:00:06.587
You'll explain why the guide runs
its steps out of numeric order.

3
00:00:06.587 --> 00:00:09.308
You'll decide each
function on its own gate,

4
00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:14.125
and record the decision with a dated
availability quote and exit criteria.

5
00:00:14.125 --> 00:00:18.888
You'll name the reference architecture's
seven zones and planes, and who owns each.

6
00:00:18.888 --> 00:00:22.369
You'll export the configuration
as hashed evidence,

7
00:00:22.369 --> 00:00:25.850
and say why the beta network
access A P I is run by hand.

8
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:30.337
And you'll turn on the four network log
categories and check that each is fresh.

9
00:00:30.337 --> 00:00:34.954
Before you start, read Network and
Transport, chapter five, for the gates,

10
00:00:34.954 --> 00:00:40.275
and skim Security Operations and Telemetry,
chapter three, for the log categories.

11
00:00:40.275 --> 00:00:43.490
The lab runs in a test
tenant, never production.
